      "AUNT MARCH: The decadents have ruined Paris, if you ask me. These French women couldn’t lift a hairbrush.\nAUNT MARCH: AMY! I said, “These French women couldn’t lift a hairbrush.”\nAMY: Oh yes! Very true, Aunt March.\nAUNT MARCH: Don’t humor me, girl. What do they write, your troublemaking family?",
      "AMY: It’s Laurie!\nAUNT MARCH: I know.",
      "MEG: Fifty dollars, what was I thinking?\nDAISY AND DEMI: Mommy -- mommy!",
      "MEG: I know just who I’ll dance with!\nAMY: Who will you dance with, Jo?\nJO: You know I never dance.\nBETH: I can’t dance.",
      "MEG: Don’t stare, don’t put your hands behind your back, don’t say Christopher Columbus, don’t say Capital, don’t shake hands, don’t whistle --\nSALLIE: Meg March! You look so pretty!\nJO: Meg..."
    ]
